    "text": {
      "excerpt": "On this pageLearn Node.js Welcome to the Node.js learning resources. Whether you're just getting started or looking to deepen your knowledge, these guides cover everything from the basics to advanced topics. Getting Started — Install Node.js and write your first program Command Line — Run scripts, use the REPL, and handle I/O HTTP — Build web servers and work with HTTP File System — Read, write, and manipulate files Asynchronous Work — Understand async patterns, promises, and the event loop Concurrency — Compare child processes, worker threads, and cluster TypeScript — Use TypeScript with Node.js Package Management — Publish and manage packages Diagnostics — Debug performance and memory issues Testing — Write and run tests with the built-in test runner Security — Follow security best practices",
